  "summary": "pypdf: Possible large memory usage for streams with multiple filters",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large memory consumption. This requires accessing any stream with a large amount of filters or multiple filters which pass around large amounts of data.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.20.0](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.20.0).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4173](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4173).",
